/-!
# Generation by `r` global sections across `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`, site by site

Let `S` be a scheme, `𝓕` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module and `r` a natural number.  Descent,
Lemma 05VG says that `𝓕` is generated by `r` global sections (Modules on Sites,
Definition 03DE (4)) if and only if `𝓕^a` is generated by `r` global sections as an `𝒪`-module,
at each of the comparison functors `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` of Descent, Proposition 03DX.  On both sides the
condition is `SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard`, the predicate registered under
Stacks 03DE "generated by r global sections": on the left it is read over the structure sheaf
`𝒪_S` of `S`, on the right over the structure sheaf of the site carrying `𝓕^a`.

This file states that equivalence once for each site, with the topology a concrete constructor.

| site | declaration |
|---|---|
| `(Sch/S)_Zar` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski` |
| `(Sch/S)_étale` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_baseAssociatedModule_etale` |
| `(Sch/S)_smooth` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_baseAssociatedModule_smooth` |
| `(Sch/S)_syntomic` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_baseAssociatedModule_syntomic` |
| `(Sch/S)_fppf` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_baseAssociatedModule_fppf` |
| `S_Zar` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_smallZariskiAssociatedModule` |
| `S_étale` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_smallEtaleAssociatedModule` |
| `S_smooth` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_smooth` |
| `S_syntomic` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_syntomic` |
| `S_fppf` | `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_fppf` |

All names are in the namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski`
  and its four siblings: the clause on the big site `(Sch/S)_τ`, at the functor
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_smallZariskiAssociatedModule`
  and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_smallEtaleAssociatedModule`:
  the clause on `S_Zar` and on `S_étale`, at `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.associatedModule` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule`.
* `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_fppf` (in
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG`) and its two siblings: the clause on the small smooth,
  syntomic and fppf sites, at `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.associatedModule`.

## Implementation notes

Each statement is specialised from the statement for its family of sites:
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_baseAssociatedModule` for
every topology of the big site,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_associatedModule` for
every flat small site,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_associatedModule` on
`S_Zar` (where quasi-coherence is not needed) and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_associatedModule` on
`S_étale`.  Those statements are about the same predicate on both sides, so no translation
between predicates is needed.  None of them assumes an equivalence: the comparison functors are
fully faithful on quasi-coherent modules by the constructions of 03DX, and every hypothesis on
`𝓕` beyond quasi-coherence is proved.

The source's small sites are `S_Zar` and `S_étale`; the small smooth, syntomic and fppf sites are
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite`, whose objects are the schemes over `S` whose structure
morphism is smooth, syntomic, or flat and locally of finite presentation.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

public section

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG

/-! ### The big sites `(Sch/S)_τ` -/

section Big

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG, "generated by `r` global sections", on `(Sch/S)_Zar`.**  A
quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module `𝓕` is generated by `r` global sections if and only if `𝓕^a` is
generated by `r` global sections as an `𝒪`-module on the big Zariski site of `S`. -/
@[stacks 05VG "generated by r global sections, big site (Sch/S)_Zar"]
theorem isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski (𝓕 : S.Modules)
    [h𝓕 : 𝓕.IsQuasicoherent] (r : ℕ) :
    SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard (R := S.ringCatSheaf) 𝓕 r ↔
      SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard
        ((BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule B S hS .zariski).obj 𝓕) r :=
  BigFppfOver.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_baseAssociatedModule B S hS .zariski ⟨𝓕, h𝓕⟩ r

